          "whyItBreaks": "The head removes `.replace(\"{{FOCUS}}\", bundle.focus ?? \"(none)\")` from the deep-prompt build (and also removes `focus: bundle.focus` from mapBundle at lines 86-88). deep.md's contract still ends with `Focus: {{FOCUS}} (if not \"(none)\", prioritize findings in that area)`, so the rendered deep prompt now ships the literal token `{{FOCUS}}` instead of the user's lens, and map.md's documented rule ('If a `focus` field is set (not null), rank matching surfaces higher') can never match because focus is no longer in the map bundle. The `--focus` option and Bundle.focus remain live (small-review path still forwards the whole bundle), so focus still works for small PRs but is silently ignored for large PRs — exactly where the large path runs. This is a contract drift: the deep.md carrier promises focus prioritization, the body no longer supplies it."
